

# <type>(<scope>)<!>: <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
#
# Examples:
#   feat: add CEX card discovery mechanism
#   
#   Implement automatic discovery of CEX cryptographic cards
#   on the host system. This enables dynamic allocation without
#   manual configuration.
#   
#   Signed-off-by: Jane Doe <jane@example.com>
#   
#   ---
#   
#   fix(kata): resolve device allocation race condition
#   
#   Signed-off-by: John Smith <john@example.com>
#
#
# --- Full Commit Message Guidelines ---
#
# Format derived from Conventional Commits v1.0.0:
# https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
# Type (Required - Conventional Commits):
#   feat     - A new feature
#   fix      - A bug fix
#   docs     - Documentation only changes
#   style    - Code style changes (formatting, missing semi colons, etc)
#   refactor - Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   test     - Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   chore    - Changes to build process or auxiliary tools
#   perf     - Performance improvements
#   ci       - Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#
# Scope (Optional - Conventional Commits + Project Specific):
#   driver   - Core DRA driver functionality
#   kata     - Kata container integration  
#   kubevirt - KubeVirt VMI integration
#   api      - API definitions and interfaces
#   config   - Configuration handling
#   tests    - Test-related changes
#   ...      - Any other ... single word, lowercase
#
# ! (Optional - Conventional Commits):
#   - mark a commit as BREAKING CHANGE
#
# Subject (Kubernetes contributor guide):
#   - 50 characters or less (hard limit: 72 chars)
#   - Capitalize first word (unless starts with lowercase symbol)
#   - No period at end
#   - Use imperative mood ("add" not "added")
#   Source: https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md
#
# Body (Optional - Kubernetes + Go project standards):
#   - Separate from subject with blank line
#   - Wrap at 72 characters
#   - Explain what and why, not how
#   - Use present tense
#   Source: https://go.dev/wiki/CommitMessage
#
# Footer (REQUIRED - DCO):
#   Signed-off-by: Firstname Lastname <email@example.com>
#   - Certifies compliance with Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO)
#   - https://developercertificate.org/
#   - Use: git commit -s or add manually
#   Source: https://go.dev/wiki/CommitMessage
#
# What NOT to include (Kubernetes guidelines):
#   - No @mentions (use PR descriptions instead)
#   - No "Address review comments" type messages
#
# To use this template: git config commit.template .gitmessage
